      ":question/id": "3fca9bbb-c820-579a-91ba-addcd4437f36",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-341757",
      ":question/problem": "If $x=-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(-14,1).$\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2y\\cdot {y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){y}^{-3/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =6{y}^{-3/2}-3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{y\\sqrt{y}}-3\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-3{y}^{2}}{y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{y\\sqrt{y}}{6-3{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(-14,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)} & =\\frac{1\\sqrt{1}}{6-3(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
